<p>I began playing Pickleball the last few years of High School. My mother discovered it and wanted our family to try it out. 
    This was around 2019, and Pickleball was not very popular at the time. I then went on my mission and played ever so often but mostly forgot 
    about it. Coming back to Utah in 2023 presented me with a completely different scene. Pickleball managed to blow up and I wanted to 
    join the hype.
</p>

<p>Now, in 2023, I compete in tournament with my brother in-law and play frequently over the summer. The rating system goes from 2.0-7.0 roughly. 
    My goal is to reach a 5.0 rating, which is the standard of a semi-pro. Currently I am a 4.0 so I have a ways to go, but I am determined to reach that goal. 
    I have been playing for about 4 years now and I have loved every minute of it.
</p>

<p>
Pickleball in general is very popular in Utah. There are many courts and many people playing. I have found that it is a great way to stay active and socialize with friends. 
    It is also a great way to relieve stress and have fun. I would highly recommend it to anyone looking for a new hobby or a way to stay active.
</p>